  "notes": "{支度|したく} refers to personal preparation — getting ready to go out, preparing for a meal, or preparing oneself for something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {支度|したく}をする / {支度|したく}する: to get ready, to prepare\n- {出|で}かける{支度|したく}: preparations to go out\n- {食事|しょくじ}の{支度|したく}: meal preparation\n- {旅|たび}の{支度|したく}: travel preparation\n- {身|み}{支度|じたく}: personal grooming, getting dressed\n\nKANJI VARIANT:\nAlso written as {仕度|したく}. Both spellings are standard.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {準備|じゅんび}: preparation (general, broader scope)\n- {用意|ようい}: preparation, readiness (more about having things ready)\n- {身|み}なり: appearance, personal grooming",
